---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Our approach — Papua Open Source"
  description="Useful work, shared source, and room to make something of your own. Learn how we approach building for Papua."
>
  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p>
      <h1>
        We make things.
        <br />
        You can take a look.
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        We like building things for Papua. Sharing how they work is part of the
        fun.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story narrow">
      <h2>See how it works.</h2>
      <p>
        Open the code, try something, and see what happens. Use whatever helps
        you learn, including AI. Just take the time to understand what you’ve
        made and check that it works.
      </p>
      <h2>Keep the idea in focus.</h2>
      <p>
        We’ve got ideas about where each project should go. We listen to
        feedback, then work out what fits and what we can look after.
      </p>
      <h2>Want to try it another way?</h2>
      <p>
        Your needs might be different from ours. If the license allows it, take
        a copy, change things, and see where your idea goes.
      </p>
      <h2>Check the license first.</h2>
      <p>
        We like sharing code, but not every project has the same rules. Open
        source and source-available licenses differ, so check the license in the
        repository before reusing or sharing a version of your own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Come see what we’re making.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Explore the projects and the stories behind them.</p>
      <a class="action" href="/projects/">
        Explore our projects
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
